<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bertrand of Baux</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1181</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Bertrand I of Baux</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bertrand of Baux was a Provençal lord of the house of Baux who acquired the principality of Orange through his marriage to Tiburge, heiress of the lords of Orange. Recognised as prince by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, he founded a line of Baux princes that ruled Orange for more than two centuries, until it passed by marriage to the house of Chalon. He was murdered in 1181.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bertrand-of-baux.jpg" alt="Bertrand of Baux" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sceau_baux-orange.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
